// The C symbol a systems builtin call is emitted under.
//
// A systems builtin (peek8, str_of_mem, ...) is normally the host runtime's
// `id_<name>` helper. A --runtime tree that defines one of these names itself
// has its own definition emitted as `idr_<name>` (fn_sym), and a call from the
// tree must reach that one: the host helper checks addresses against the host's
// store, while the tree's functions work on the tree's own arena. So when
// fn_sym renames the name, the call follows it; any other name keeps the helper
// sys_helper_at picked (including the width-suffixed and renamed ones).

sys_sym(int id) {
  string sym_n = (import ns1)[id];
  string sym_h = sys_helper_at(id);
  if(fn_sym(sym_n) != "id_" + sym_n) {
    sym_h = fn_sym(sym_n);
  }
} return string sym_h;
